    description: "Open question from ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04072026_1355.md 'Open Questions / Followups' §5: should the bakeoff harness gain a 'linker prospect' cohort that runs dead-code-maybe on the polyglot subset of the curriculum?\n\nThe notebook explicitly recommends framing the experiment as a one-shot prospecting run ('Retire the pipeline. The marginal value of the 5th rerun is much lower than the 1st; the long tail is dominated by reflection / framework issues that need different fixes.') So this item may resolve as 'wont_do'.\n\nDecide YES/NO after the triage item completes and we know whether the signal stays useful over time. If YES: add a new cohort/curriculum definition under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/curricula/ that selects polyglot repos from the pool and runs the prospector via bakeoff-broad or bakeoff-deep.\n\nDepends on the initial triage pass producing a clear judgment on reusability."  # e123
